// #1372 review (Codex P1): the compiler-generated entry boundary
// (linked_compile.vibe's lc_wrap_entry_error_boundary) catches the ERASED
// `Error::Throw`, and under ADR-0085 that arm also catches every typed
// `Exception[E]` -- the runtime carries a single abortive tag with NO kind
// discriminator, and the erased `Error` spelling is deliberately compatible
// with every kind (that is what made #1344 additive).
//
// So the payload bound here is an ENUM, not a String. Writing it straight to
// `Stderr::write_stream` decoded the enum pointer as a packed `(ptr<<32)|len`
// string and printed the whole data segment (measured: ~1KB of unrelated
// identifier bytes for a `TaskError` escaping `main`). PR #1375 routed it
// through `__to_string` instead -- bounded, but it printed a bare decimal
// with nothing to say it was not the message.
//
// #1374 gave the throw site a kind side channel, so the boundary can now name
// what escaped. Pinned behaviour: exit 1, exactly
//
//   vibe: uncaught error: <Boom>
//
// on stderr. The paired err_entry_boundary_string_payload.vibe pins the other
// side: a String payload still prints verbatim.
//
// Printing the VALUE of a non-String payload is still out of reach -- that
// needs per-kind formatting, not just a kind name.
enum Boom {
  Bang(Int)
}

fn main() -> Int with Exception {
  throw(Bang(7))
}
